# Here i used simple KQL to see who was the CEO using simple KQL
Kusto Query Language (KQL) - Kusto Query Language (KQL) is a powerful tool for exploring
my data and discovering patterns, identifying anomalies and outliers. This language is used by Cyber Security Analysts Backend Developers.

### here is a baisc KQL script
Employees 
| where role == "CEO"

-As you can see 'Employees' I can use this to get the data of EMployees for the company
- Then use | to find the source of data
- Then i use pipeline character *'|'*, 
- After that I then add *'where'* operator 
-Now I use a column aka the *'role'* 
- Then now use compsriosn operator like equality operater and value *'=="CEO"* ' 
-I get to employee needed which is the CEO
- Important note KQL is casse sensitive
